    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="0810" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/15122b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Brazilian Minister to Mexico.</hi><anchor
                        n="23" xml:id="d887-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-02T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1915—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>741. You will please lay before the Mexico City authorities for their information
                    the following public statement just issued by the President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d887-a1.xml" xpointer="d887-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d887-f1" n="23" type="source" xml:id="d887-f1-content">
                <p>The statement of the President was also telegraphed to all American Consuls and
                    other representatives in Mexico, for publication.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
